# b8_ot_instances_1: paid phase, rank 5 by rule 6
#
# faithful line (2026-09-30, impl/patches/faithful_nonlinear.py); b7_ot_instances_2 peak
# 1,796,776 kB, grouped by allocating function, share of attributed total:
#   heap:_M_invoke  <- buffer.h:44 (discriminator 2):yacl::Buffer:    402.7 MB  0.220
#   heap:BasicOTProtocols::BasicOTProtocols(std::shared_ptr<>, spu    335.6 MB  0.184
#   heap:BasicOTProtocols::BasicOTProtocols(std::shared_ptr<>, spu    335.6 MB  0.184
#   heap:MatMatProtocol::EncodeMatrixSlice<>(spu::NdArrayRef const     63.2 MB  0.035
#   heap:spu::Value spu::dynDispatch<>(spu::SPUContext*, std::__cx     56.6 MB  0.031
# Numbers below: earlier placeholder-nonlinearity line (not published), same objects, same order.
# basis      Ferret OT buffer at the predecessor's peak (~1600 MB on the placeholder line).
# impl_lever: none
# No source change; BB_MAX_CONCURRENCY below.
# pool_attacked: host

#
# lever      BB_MAX_CONCURRENCY 2 -> 1 (OT instances in CheetahOTState); OMP_NUM_THREADS stays 16
#            (unlike the earlier line's one-thread run). Instance = Ferret sender + receiver adapter,
#            160 MiB each: -320 MiB.
# guard      op_bench announces CONFIG|rank=N|...|max_concurrency=<value>; harness writes
#            bb_max_concurrency into RUN_META; both checked after harvest.
# manifest   BB_MAX_CONCURRENCY was pinned with OMP_NUM_THREADS on a core-count argument that
#            applies only to the latter; correction and sweep in MANIFEST.md.
# floor      target OT term = one instance (2 x 167,772,160 B = 335,544,320 B, MANIFEST.md): axis
#            closed after this step.
# cost       paid, extrapolated from the sweep: -704 MiB for +66.2% wall = 11 MiB per %.
# caveat     transcript +0.62 to 0.74 MB per instance removed (constant over four points; Ferret
#            setup, online phase unchanged), ~1000x the ~2e-6 within-step spread.
# object_attacked: BasicOTProtocols::BasicOTProtocols
#
# key        re-declared after the depth-5 re-measurement (2026-08-13); caller half of the
#            (caller, allocating function) key.
# measured   -320.0 MB.
OMP_NUM_THREADS=16
BB_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
